<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Estonian Defence League</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1918">1918</a>–<a href="/years/1940">1940</a>, <a href="/years/1990">1990</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Kaitseliit</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Estonian Defence League, or Kaitseliit, is a voluntary armed national defence organisation founded in November 1918 during the War of Independence. It grew into a large militia in the interwar republic and was dissolved after the Soviet occupation in 1940. Re-established in 1990, it now forms part of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>'s defence forces with a large volunteer membership.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/estonian-defence-league.jpg" alt="Estonian Defence League" width="320" height="289" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: unknown; Quibik · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kaitseliit_emblem.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
